Solve Equations With Logarithms

COMMON ERROR
Remember that 10 is not a coefficient, but a base. You cannot divide both sides by 10 and then add 1 to solve for x.

What is the solution to each equation? Round to the nearest thousandth.

A. 25 = 10^{x-1}
\begin{align*}
25 &= 10^{x-1} 
\log 25 &= x - 1 ([IMAGE: Callout: Convert to logarithmic form.]) 
1 + \log 25 &= x 
2.398 &≈ x
\end{align*}

B. \ln (2x + 3) = 4
\begin{align*}
\ln (2x + 3) &= 4 
2x + 3 &= e^4 ([IMAGE: Callout: Convert to exponential form.]) 
2x + 3 &≈ 54.598 
2x &≈ 51.598 
x &≈ 25.799
\end{align*}
